{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (via the cobbler orchestrator) assigned task #5271: implement srd024-expand requirements R4.1, R4.2, and R4.3. These are differential testing requirements for the `cmd/expand` utility:\n   - **R4.1**: Differential tests must compare Go expand output against `gexpand` byte-for-byte via `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests`\n   - **R4.2**: Tests must cover: default tab expansion, `-t N` with a single interval, `-t LIST` with multiple tab stops, input with no tabs (passthrough), and multiple tabs in succession\n   - **R4.3**: Tests must use `LC_ALL=C` to eliminate locale-dependent divergence\n   \n   The task specifies modifying `cmd/expand/main.go` and creating/updating `cmd/expand/expand_test.go`. No git commands should be run.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing pattern using `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` comparing Go binary vs GNU reference binary (`gexpand`)\n   - `testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")` to compile the Go binary under test\n   - `exec.LookPath(\"gexpand\")` with `t.Skip` if reference not found\n   - `DiffTest` struct: `{ Name, Args, Stdin, Env, WorkDir, ExitCode, Normalize, ExpectedFiles }`\n   - `LC_ALL=C` environment variable for locale-independent testing\n   - SIGPIPE handling via `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - Tab stop expansion with uniform intervals and absolute position lists\n   - The shared_protocols state \"The harness sets LC_ALL=C by default\"\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd024-expand.yaml**\n     - The SRD specification defining all requirements R1-R4\n     - R4.1-R4.3 are the differential testing requirements assigned to this task\n     - Non-goals: no backspace handling, no Unicode grapheme width (